comments.body:
@fpietrosanti for kodi, going full https would mean we'd have 3x server CPU load because the overhead of the TLS handshake is huge, specially if you have very short lived sessions almost exclusively.
Our current hardware is not able to handle this.

@etix my idea for "selective" https on the mirror side would be a configureable path prefix that tells mirrorbits to only serve https.
e.g.
- securePathPrefix=/sslonly/

@MartijnKaijser to sum up, you'd like a way to tell mirrorbits that for a given request it should only return HTTPS mirrors? Would a query argument be fine?

@fpietrosanti the mirrorbits project has no leverage over mirrors, we have no way to force mirrors to use HTTPS. They will all do the switch eventually.

@wsnipex that is a valid option but I have a preference for specifying this per-request instead of marking a whole path as HTTPS only but I'm open to the discussion.
